abstract: >-
  Lean 4 formalization (Lean v4.30.0-rc1, Mathlib 0c154d67103f74be3a0f2c509f72ccbf5be9f2a7) and
  paper. For the velocity-slot Frohmanian tether with pointwise vorticity weight,
  B(a,b) = -kappa * int |omega|^2 (Pi_u a . Pi_u b), on T^3, the correction generated by the
  kinetic energy vanishes identically (Pi_u u = 0). Hence the metriplectic tether model has the
  same weak right-hand side and the same smooth solutions as the Navier-Stokes equations on T^3,
  for every kappa and nu, and its global regularity is equivalent to Navier-Stokes global
  regularity on T^3, which remains open. Also proved: the L2 gradient of the energy is u; the
  tether is negative semidefinite and equals -4 pi^2 kappa at an explicit Beltrami state, so it is
  not a metric bracket; the factorized-weight variant has the same degeneracy. Not a Clay
  Millennium Problem proof. Main theorem locked by a Truth Gate semantics lock; all theorems
  depend only on propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound.
